{"name":"Center Field","hex":"#008b56","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"center field","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of a baseball field which is beyond the infield and straight ahead left if you stand on home plate and face the pitcher.","The defensive position in the outfield in the middle, typically played by a player that can run fast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/center_field"}],"entries":[{"title":"Center fielder","blocks":[{"text":"A center fielder, abbreviated CF, is the outfielder in baseball who plays defense in center field – the baseball and softball fielding position between left field and right field. In the numbering system used to record defensive plays, the center fielder is assigned the number 8."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Baseball_CF.svg/330px-Baseball_CF.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Center_fielder","wikidata":"Q5059480"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Minute_Maid_Park_Centerfield.JPG/500px-Minute_Maid_Park_Centerfield.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Minute_Maid_Park_Centerfield.JPG/1280px-Minute_Maid_Park_Centerfield.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Minute_Maid_Park_Centerfield.JPG/500px-Minute_Maid_Park_Centerfield.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View from center field at Daikin Park.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinute_Maid_Park_Centerfield.JPG"}],"sounds":{"center field":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/68/En-au-center_field.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaig